      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town grew after a 100‑foot railroad right‑of‑way was sold to the Choctaw, Oklahoma Railroad in 1903, leading to a boom in stores, churches, and a hotel.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        10,
        21,
