      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/vega-tx",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Vega Public Library, built in 1911, once housed a silent‑movie theater and now holds about 11,000 books.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vega%2C_Texas",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "When Route 66 arrived, Vega developed tourist courts, gas stations, and shops to serve travelers on the Mother Road.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
